WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
Connect a battery across a metal rod.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.270
Charge starts to drift along it.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.560
A rod carrying a current is not
in electrostatic equilibrium.

4
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.590
There is an electric
field inside the metal.

5
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.380
In a uniform rod, that field has
the same strength from end to end.

6
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.830
Now make the rod conduct
less well towards one end.

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.540
Where along it is the field strongest?

8
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.060
In this mission, you'll
meet current density:

9
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.600
the current per unit
area, with a direction.

10
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.960
Then you'll add up current
ring by ring across a wire,

11
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.440
and resistance slice by slice along a rod.

12
00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.340
Your mission: predict where along
the rod the field is strongest,

13
00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.560
and explain why.
